We've got to wean you off of the Orcish and the Wizard. Wizard is no
doubt one of the easiest classes to ascend (my first two ascensions
were Wiz-Neu-Hum-Mal), and with racial bonuses it's even easier. But to
start another class and race when you've been playing a single
combination for so long will be difficult, so I suggest you go for an
elven Wizard.

You'll still get the chaotic benefits, infravision, and goodies, only
exchanging poison resistance and cannabalism for sleep resistance and
20 intelligence. After that, do a human Wizard, and then go from there.

What next? There'll be a wide range to choose from, but you should
probably stick to a spellcasting class. Go for a Tourist or a Priest,
then choose a Knight or a Samurai. By then, you'll be proficient enough
to play any class well. Just don't get discouraged if you fail the
first several (or hundred) times; keep trying and eventually you'll get
there.

Good luck!



